    "metadata": {
      "title": "Benign Memory Contamination in LLM Agents: A Taxonomy, Benchmark, and Contract-Level Mitigations",
      "repository": "https://github.com/arananet/contam-bench",
      "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22859806"
    },
    "thesis": [
      "We propose a taxonomy of six mechanisms by which ordinary memory-system behaviour, with no attacker or poisoned record, could degrade later responses, each with a falsifiable contamination criterion: semantic drift, provenance collapse, scope bleed, temporal staleness, recursive compounding and summarization loss. The pilot exercises a subset of them; the taxonomy is a conceptual contribution, not an empirical result."
    ],
